// THE WITNESS THIS REPOSITORY DID NOT HAVE, and three released versions went out
// without it. v0.1.453 settled an undecided allocation region on the CALLER's -- which
// the backends lower to the runtime current region -- on the argument that a call does
// not change the current region, so inside the callee it must be the region open around
// the call. `dune runtest`, parity, every gate and all 29 dogfood type-checks were green
// and m3d could not render a second frame. Withdrawn in v0.1.456. Verified: built at
// 62e1858 (v0.1.455), this program prints 700 on the interpreter and -424242 on C.
//
// WHAT SEPARATES THE TWO ANSWERS IS A CHAIN, and the shape below is the smallest one:
//
//   * `cache` is a TOP-LEVEL container, so its element region is a monomorphic variable
//     shared with a global. The call-site rule only binds a callee's QUANTIFIED
//     allocation regions -- a refinement that exists because binding a shared one
//     retypes the global (mere-ruby's frame pool was the false positive that found it).
//     So nothing binds this one.
//   * `leaf` allocates. Its region reaches `cache`'s through `fill_cache`, so it is that
//     same unquantified variable, and it stays undecided all the way to codegen.
//   * `top 700` is the only call written inside `region A { }`. The allocation happens
//     three frames down, where no region is lexically active.
//
// Settled on `__heap` -- what it means today -- the value goes to the default region and
// survives the block, which is what the interpreter, C and LLVM all print. Settled on
// the runtime current region it goes into A's arena, `region B` reuses that arena, and
// the read comes back as whatever B left there. The type says neither: it says `__heap`
// in both cases, so no escape check can fire. Only running it tells them apart.
//
// `region B` is not decoration. An arena is REUSED rather than freed, so without a
// second block that allocates over it the stale pointer still reads 700 and the bug
// looks absent. ASan is blind to it too: the arena is one live allocation. The value it
// scribbles is deliberately unmistakable rather than -1.
//
// WASM ANSWERED -424242 HERE FOR ONE AFTERNOON, and that is why this file has four
// matching columns rather than three and a pin. Wasm has ONE bump pointer for every
// region, so an allocation made anywhere during a block -- by a callee, three frames
// down, with a type that says the default region -- was inside the block's range and
// was rolled back with it. The backend's guard rejected escaping stores it could SEE
// and could not see through a call. Recorded as Q-132 and pinned to the wrong answer;
// the fix (v0.1.458) gave the block a high-water mark, the pin went stale, and parity
// said so by name. The pin is gone and this case is an ordinary four-way MATCH.
let cache = vec_new ();
let leaf = fn (n: int) -> let v = vec_new () in let _ = vec_push v n in v;
let fill_cache = fn (n: int) -> vec_push cache (leaf n);
let mid = fn (n: int) -> fill_cache n;
let top = fn (n: int) -> mid n;

// Enough pushes to walk past the first chunk of the arena A used.
let rec scribble = fn (v) -> fn (i: int) ->
  if i >= 4096 then 0 else let _ = vec_push v (0 - 424242) in scribble v (i + 1);

let _ = region A { top 700 };
let _ = region B { let junk = vec_new () in scribble junk 0 };

print_int (vec_get (vec_get cache 0) 0)
